    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n41054" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rĕ-mōlĭor</span></b> ,
			ītus, 4, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>v. dep. a.</i>, <i>to
			press</i>, <i>push</i>, or <i>move
			back</i> or <i>away</i> (<b>poet.</b> and in post-Aug. prose): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">saepe remoliri luctatur pondera terrae
					(Typhoëus),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					5, 354</span></i>
			; so, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ferrea claustra,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					Th. 10, 527</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Sen. Q. N. 6, 13 <i>fin.</i></span></i>— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>To stir</i> or <i>take up again</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">arma,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sil. 1,
					36</span></i>
			.?*! <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rĕmōlītus</span></b> , a,
			um, <i>pass.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">orbe remolito,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Herc. Fur. 504</span></i>
			.</div>
